      "content": "it feels more than just pressure though. it's like i'm watching a movie of my own life and i'm not even the main character anymore. i see the mistakes happening, i see the dignity slipping away every time i stumble or stare blankly at someone. it's terrifying to think about being years into this, just being a burden that doesn't even know where it is. i'd rather just... stop the clock now, while i can still at least recognize myself. i don't want to wait until i'm just a ghost in my own body.",
